criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

1. ART use \>12 months;
2. Viral load \<200 copies/mL;
3. Stable use (\>90 days) of moderate-intensity statin (pitavastatin 4mg daily, atorvastatin 10-20mg daily, rosuvastatin 5-10mg daily; simvastatin 20-40mg; pravastatin 40-80mg) or maximally tolerated statin if prior history of statin intolerance;
4. ASCVD risk ≥5%;
5. Baseline TBR≥2.3 on cardiac 18F-FDG-PET

Exclusion Criteria:

1. MRA use within the last 90 days;
2. Use of potassium (K) supplements;
3. Known HFrEF or primary aldosteronism;
4. Known Addison's disease
5. Use of ritonavir, nelfinavir, clarithromycin, and other strong inhibitors of CYP3A4 and CYP3A4 inducers (boosting doses of ritonavir 100mg are allowed);
6. Use of potassium-sparing diuretic;
7. Steroids or other anti-inflammatory agents within last 1 month; NSAIDs are allowed;
8. Newly initiated GLP1-RA or anti-hypertensive within 90 days, stable use \>90 days is allowed;
9. SBP\<90mmHg;
10. Type 1 DM or poorly controlled type 2 DM with HbA1c\>7.5%;
11. Creatinine (Cr)\>1.5 mg/dL or eGFR\<60mL/min/1.73m²;
12. K\>5.5 mEq/L;
13. Hemoglobin\<10.0 g/dL;
14. Pregnant, seeking pregnancy, breastfeeding;
15. Active infection (besides HIV);
16. Significant radiation exposure from clinical or research scans, cumulative exposure ≥25mSv over 12 months is not allowed;
17. Iodine contrast allergy;
18. Known severe coronary artery stenosis, defined as ≥50% stenosis in the left main coronary artery or \>70% stenosis
